I think this means that this game stretched out over 30
months. I started one night on a business trip, just to see
if I could do the protection racket I had seen discussed
here. Good thing I keep good notes!

This was the starting character:

Laslo the Rhizotomist   St:9 Dx:8 Co:16 In:11 Wi:15 Ch:16 
Neutral
Dlvl:1  $:1560 HP:13(13) Pw:6(6) AC:8  Xp:1/0 T:134

The protection racket was a bit more of a test since the
entrance to the mines was on DL 4 but Minetown was only on
DL 7. Somehow I accidentally tried on some cursed gloves. I
got a nymph to relieve me of them but later she came back
for my elven cloak. The problem was soon solved by my
faithful cat, Lucy.

The temple was cross aligned and there wasn't a general
store or a bookstore in the game which made identification
more of a problem. Later in the game I was throwing things
in the shops to get the shopkeeper to "own" it and then
buying things back. I came out of Minetown with a -7 AC
which is great for this part of the game.

The entrance to Sokoban was on DL 6. I had a difficult
battle with a party of green elves here. Sokoban yielded up
an "oR and 3 points of much needed strength. A cockatrice
had me slowing down but I had a LC handy to save that near
death.

Back in the mines, I hit a poly trap and became a new woman,
losing two XLs and two points of strength gaining some Dx in
the deal.

