By this point in the game I had gain the following
intrinsics: fire, telepathy, poison, cold, sleep and speed.
I didn't get disintegration resistance until 35755 and shock
resistance until 46118.

There was a master mind flayer on Level 10 of the mines and
a mind flayer on Level 11! One of my cats fell victim to the
mind flayer.

Back in the main dungeon, I found a neutral temple on DL9
and emptied 2 /oCM getting several four leaf clovers but
nothing to fight with. By this time I was using a unicorn
horn which was my weapon of choice until after I got my
quest artifact, the Staff of Aesculapius. There were five
temples in this game so most of the gold was donated 6 times
resulting, ultimately, in 17 points of protection.

On DL 14 there was a huge turning point in the game.
Normally, once I have gotten this far I wouldn't need a
wish, but a Throne Wish tempted me. I have never had the
Eyes of the Overworld and it sounded like fun so I went for
it on the principle that I should chose my conducts based on
what makes the game more interesting for me. So I got the
Eyes. Moments later, I was offered a second wish from the
same throne. What the heck, let's have the Eye of the
Aethiopica for getting around the dungeon and doing some
spell casting!

Soon afterward I saw a post by Boudewijn where he said he
accepted throne, fountain and potion wishes but not lamp or
wand wishes or something to that effect. I thought that
sounded pretty good, the castle wand makes ascending pretty
much a slam dunk but these other wishes might interject some
variety instead of just making you invulnerable. As an
additional challenge since I had abandoned the wishless
conduct, I decided to do no alchemy and to hold my HP down
to something around 200 instead of the 350 to 600 available
with a bit of easy alchemy.

A poly trap, a large cat and a magic whistle got me a pet I
kept until just before the run for the amulet, a pit fiend
that ended up looking like this:

Status of Bart (chaotic):  Level 19  HP 148(152)  AC -10,
tame, fast.
