Tools
f - a unicorn horn

And I did enjoy the message when he fell in a pit! :)

DL 15 had the entrance to Ludious. I cleared the front rooms
and the Fort outer grounds but didn't feel ready for the
Fort itself just yet. Later when I used the Eye to portal
back I was surprised to land in the treasure room with all
the gold and traps! I thought when you teleported to a
special level you always entered in the part of the level
you would have arrived at through natural means.

I was planning to stand a knight's move from the door and
fight the monsters one at a time. Well a stone giant got
into it with Bart in the doorway and Bart got the best of
him. A boulder fell in the doorway and a much better plan
presented itself. Magic Missile and Drain Life were fired
from behind the boulder until power was exhausted, then I
would gather treasure for a while and repeat!

This is the first time I've used Drain Life extensively,
it's a really nice little spell. Particularly for trolls or
something you may want to weaken now and come back later
with more power.

By the time I reached Medusa's level I still had no way to
levitate or water walk. I did have the jump spell and the
Eye if needed to get back up so I dug through. I was
surprised when I came back up that I had to fight Medusa. I
was wearing a blindfold and an "oR and thought she would
immediately be stoned when I came up the stairs but instead
I had to beat her to death. Perseus statue did have
levitation boot which were promptly zapped with my /oCancel.

At the castle I used a ?oEarth to plug the moat, zapped the
drawbridge with a /oStriking and retreated to the maze to
fight one on one. I got a +2 CoP from the armory and a set
of silver scales from one of the dragons. Since I had found
two MMs and a ?oCharging along the way I was pretty much
set. Then I got a third throne wish and I took a (BoH. I
also got [WWB either here or in the VotD.

Back to the quest now. I slipped up on the cyclops weaning
my [WWB, hit it with a sleep spell and then fired magic
missile until it died. I liked the Staff, it is a good
weapon, but it still can't compare to any wombat two
weaponing a good artifact. Since it is a two handed weapon
and I had other options I didn't plan to use it once I had
the book, but ultimately, on the astral plane, I concluded
it was better for a healer than Frost Brand or Vorpal Blade.

I still had no unholy water so at this point I went through
the whole dungeon dipping potions of water in fountains in
hopes of getting them cursed. Well, I was lucky and unlucky.
I got no unholy water (can you even do it that way?) but I
got another wish which I used for speed boots (I had been
wearing jumping boots and casting self haste). I used the
trick with a b?oRC to get my unholy water.

I fairly flew through Gehennom. I knew the magic mapping
spell well enough and I didn't need anything else but the
amulet so I would cast light and magic mapping and dig to
the next set of stairs. The Eyes enabled me to spot a few
helpful items along the way. I would actively hunt down
(m)mf's trying to help my intelligence. I didn't think
wearing a [HoB affected your ability to gain intelligence
from a (m)mf corpse but after several failures I started
removing the helm before eating the corpses and had some
success. Probably just a coincidence.

I got a scary surprise from Juiblex of all demons! I waited
for a bit for him to come around to be killed and finally
decided to swap my speed boots for WWBs. He appeared and
swallowed me immediately as I put on the WWB so several
turns went by with me ill! After that I decided maybe it was
just silly to eschew an "oLS when you had reflection AND the
Eyes.

Baalzebub was a pain, he had a /oDig so I couldn't kill him
by preempting the upstairs. Must have chased him 5 or 6
levels before he mysteriously didn't use his /oDig even
though it still had charges. Had to kill Orcus twice, he had
an "oLS! About this time I lost Bart to a purple worm
summoned by and arch lich. On DL48 of 51 I got a +3 athame
from another arch lich, Hooray!

After marking the VS and clearing Rodney's tower except for
his room, I zipped back up to do my final polishing and make
sure I had my stuff for getting through the planes quickly.
I had managed to accumulate 7 !oGL for the exit from
Gehennom and that wasn't quite enough for all the levels
with really long walks.

I never found a =oFA, =oLev, =oConflict, any shirt or any
means of TC. I ate one tengu and might have eaten Rodney at
one point but I was satiated at the time. So all those
?oTeleportation went to waste. Maybe I should've taken more
time to explore Gehennom.

Rodney wasn't a great deal of trouble but he did double
trouble me once (a first for me) and steal my quest artifact
once (another first for me) but since I was using Frost
Brand at the time it was no big deal. That first fight in
his tower I killed them with Frosty to save my /oDeath
charges, I guess I just took much longer than usual to put
him down.

The fight outside he sanctum was the most difficult I can
remember there. I slipped through the graveyard with
stealth, killing only enough to make a path, locking doors
behind me but when I arrived in the area outside the sanctum
a arch lich and a master lich dropped in and summoned stuff
faster than I could kill 'em. I felt like the Astral Plane
the way I was having to kill multiple monsters to take one
step, and I wasn't killing them very fast. When the L's came
around I would burn an Elbereth and pull out Vorpal Blade
but I never got in a lucky shot.

I did get luck that the door to the sanctum was on the
second side I searched with my /oSDD, It could have gone on
twice as long. I force bolted the door down, jumped in and
wizard locked the door behind me. Then here comes one of the
big liches. Time to move fast, zap the priest of Moloch with
a /oDeath grab the amulet and quaff a c!oGL, whew.

On the way out I still was reluctant to wield a two handed
weapon and kept my (BoH on the oilskin sack most of the
time, even so, by the end of the game my (BoH had been
unblessed 4 times (another first for me). The Staff got hit
once but resisted.

I left the dungeon at 71300 and arrived on Astral at 71693,
longer than usual for me because my normal method for
speeding the the Plane of Water failed me. I couldn't part
with all my pretty stuff in the dungeon so I decided to do
all but Astral while burdened and make a stash upon arriving
on Astral. Earth was easy. I wore [BoLev and quaff !oSpeed
through the next three planes. Air was a little scary when
my /oPoly trick only worked half the time on the air
elementals. On water, my last ?oGD located the portal but by
the time I got there it had moved too far for my /oSDD to
find it.

Arriving on Astral, I removed my [BoLev (been know to break
all those extra potions by forgetting to do that first)
burned an Elbereth, dropped my bag and waited for the
liches. That over, I got unburdened by making a little stash
in a spare sack I'd brought along. left most the !oEH,
unholy water, some holy water and most all the blank
scrolls, all the K Rations and the two spellbooks I brought
with me.

Went to see pestilence first because he was closet. This is
about as hard as I can remember the Astral Planes, I had to
use a couple of !oFH and invoke the staff once. It was just
brutal to get anywhere. I finally switched to the Staff for
my weapon and seemed to get along a bit faster than with
Frost Brand. And I wasn't fighting everything. I would use
Elbereth on those that respected it and often a
/oTeleportation on the others. Pestilence made me sick
twice. Wrong altar, back to the middle.

On the way I passed by my stash to grab some more holy
water. Well the holy water burdened me and here comes
another big lich. Dropped my bag, killed the lich and
reblessed the items I grabbed the holy water for and off I
went to the middle altar. Yeah, you guessed it, forgot my
bag and I'm going to visit Famine with 2 pancakes and a
=oSD. 

Well things were going faster, I was using the jump spell
more. Got to the altar and it's wrong again. Got a "You
Murderer" message for killing a priest that was attacking
me, must have hit him with a stray teleportation beam. The
spell casting made me hungry and Famine was coming back for
another round. I ate my two pancakes and reached for my bag
to get out more food and a fresh /oDeath. Oh, S**t.

Could I get back to my stash? Surveyed what was in
inventory. Two "oLS, a !oFH, a well charged /oTele and a
/oDeath with 2 charges and I can pray. Well obviously that
was enough. I think I only used a few charges on the
/oTeleport and one on the /oDeath. So I fought my way back
to the stash and bag, reloaded and headed for the third and
final altar.

This was the easiest of the three, I guess the overall
population of the Astral plane was diminished. When I got to
the final altar room I put a sleep spell on some ants
outside the door and wizard locked the door. Then I killed
the infidels in Hermes Temple and went to the altar. Got out
my two rings of adornment (for the party in the demigod
bar), charged the one that was +0, lit the Candelabrum of
Invocation and offered the Amulet.

And that's the story of Laslo, the only healer I've ever
played.

